					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/onemanquartet" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1329902); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1329902&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607916798" alt="OneManQuartet " style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1329902)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/onemanquartet" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1329902); return false;" >OneManQuartet </a></span> <span class="odate time_1335833094 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">01 May 2012 00:44</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1433624">
									

<p>I may have skipped over something major in the article here by accident, but is SCP-1450 really the type of anomalous the foundation would go after? I mean nothing besides being unidentified is really THAT out of the norm, even then, it could just be near extinction or something, a lot of the traits of it can be found in real life animals, In fact something very similar to this has probably existed somewhere in the universe in reality.</p>
<p>But I'm just being picky here, the idea is odd and creepy enough for that nit-picky problem to not ruin my enjoyment of the article, this gets a +1 in my metaphorical book.</p>

							</div>

								
					
