					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/arlecchino" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(341058); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=341058&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607916798" alt="Arlecchino" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=341058)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/arlecchino" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(341058); return false;" >Arlecchino</a></span> <span class="odate time_1335833404 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">01 May 2012 00:50</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1433629">
									

<p>I feel it's justified in being an SCP for several reasons:</p>
<p>A. It can eat and shit latex paint. That's theoretically something that could be evolved, but consider we only started using latex paints in the last few decades&#8230;</p>
<p>B. It hunts people. It's specifically designed to inhabit urban areas and <em>hunt humans</em>. There's a word for that: Bloody dangerous. It's two words, and now my colon is clenching a little because there's a lot of abandoned buildings around here. (What have I <em>done</em>?)</p>
<p>C. It's got no identifiable genus. That means there's nothing to tie it to the rest of the naturally evolved species on earth. This thing appears to have just POPPED into existence.</p>
<p>Given all that, I feel like the foundation would be justifiably paranoid enough to start burning it out of existence while studying a small sample.</p>

							</div>

								
					
